## BUG-05 (MEDIUM): Unix socket world-accessible
# File: main.cpp:276-290
#
# IPC socket at /tmp/neuro_mesh_{id}.sock created with no chmod() after
# bind(). Default umask (022) makes it world-writable. Any local user can
# send CMD:INJECT, CMD:ISOLATE, CMD:SHUTDOWN.
#
# Fix: chmod(socket_path, 0600) after bind().

## BUG-06 (LOW): IPC evidence buffer truncation — fencepost error
# File: main.cpp:410-429
#
# Read buffer is 65536 bytes (reads up to 65535). Evidence size validation
# allows up to 65536 bytes. After stripping "CMD:INJECT <target> " prefix,
# evidence capacity is ~65517 bytes. Evidence between ~65517-65536 bytes
# is silently truncated without the REJECT:EVIDENCE_TOO_LARGE error firing.
# Practical impact is near-zero (evidence payloads are tiny).
#
# Fix: Lower evidence limit to 65000 or reduce buffer to match validation.

